.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-webhooks-update - Update a webhook's name, callback URL, or topics


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 webhooks update  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Change a webhook's name, callback URL, or topics in place. The id and the shared
secret are kept, so the receiver keeps verifying with the secret it already has.

.PP
--topic REPLACES the whole set, which is also how a topic is REMOVED: pass the
ones you want to keep. Adding one means passing the existing topics plus the new
one, so read them first with 'webhooks get \&'.

.PP
This does NOT change whether the webhook is active. Repointing a broken webhook
at a URL that works leaves it exactly as inactive as it was — which is the
second half of the repair sequence worth knowing:
.IP "  1." 5
\&'webhooks event-callbacks  --status failed'   what was it failing on
.IP "  2." 5
\&'webhooks update  --callback-url …'           fix it
.IP "  3." 5
\&'webhooks reset-circuit \&'                     let it deliver again
.IP "  4." 5
\&'webhooks redeliver  \&'           replay what was lost

.PP
Step 3 is not optional after a tripped breaker, and doing it before step 2 just
spends another 10 events reopening it. Step 4 replays one failed attempt's
payload per call; skipping step 3 makes the replay drop silently.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-u\fP, \fB--callback-url\fP=""
	New callback URL

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update

.PP
\fB-n\fP, \fB--name\fP=""
	New webhook name

.PP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--topic\fP=[]
	REPLACE the topic set; repeat for several. Omitting a topic removes it


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 webhooks update whk_abc123 --callback-url https://example.com/new
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-webhooks(1)\fP
